SUMMARY:Sunday Brunch Revolutionary Texts Lecture Series No. 2
DESCRIPTION:Many texts containing “revolutionary ideas” have shaped American history and identity\, not just one.  Our Christian calling as citizens of this great country is to help Rejoice\, Repair and Renew our national life. In a special Sunday Brunch Lectures series in honor of the 250th anniversary of our nation’s founding\, thought-leading social historians and theologians will reflect on a range of radical texts that challenge\, expand or declare unfulfilled the rights and aspirations set forth in the Declaration of Independence. \n  \nJoin parishioner and vestry member Dr. Drew Hermeling to explore the Two Row Wampum Treaty of 1613 between the Five Nations of the Haudenosaunee (or Iroquois) and the colonial Dutch government that is spiritually and culturally important as part of indigenous social history and American socio-political understanding. \n  \nRegistration is required for catering with a suggested donation of $25 for adults. \nThe Revolutionary Texts Lecture Series continues this fall. Look for more information soon. \nRegistration deadline: Monday\, July 6th \nClick here for more info and to register.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/sunday-brunch-revolutionary-texts-lecture-series-no-2/
LOCATION:Saint James Parish House Forum Room\, 119 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Revolutionary-Text-3-copy.jpg
GEO:40.0404103;-76.303616
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Saint James Parish House Forum Room 119 North Duke Street Lancaster PA 17602 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=119 North Duke Street:geo:-76.303616,40.0404103
END:VEVENT
